    "message": "feat(analytics): record the whole route trace, and drop the bare gpt-5.6\n\nA vision diversion left no trace at all. `_apply_vision_policy` replaces the\nhead of the chain, so a diverted request was logged as provider=chatgpt_oauth,\nmodel=gpt-5.6-luna, route_attempt=0 -- byte-identical to a route that simply\npoints at that model. Three releases of vision routing were unobservable, and\nthe only fields that existed (`route_attempt`, `route_primary_model`) had no\ntest asserting they reached storage either.\n\nThe plan now carries its own decision. `RoutedMessagesPlan` gains\n`diverted_from` and `diversion` (a `RouteDiversion` enum, today only VISION),\nset when the applied policy changes the head of the chain. `RequestCapture`\ngains `set_plan()`, called once before execution by both the Messages and\nResponses handlers.\n\nThree new columns, migrated on open like every column since 4.22.0:\n\n    route_chain           every model the request was prepared to try, in order\n    route_diverted_from   the route's own model, when a policy replaced it\n    route_diversion       which policy did it\n\n`route_chain` is stored even when the primary answers: \"a chain existed and was\nnot needed\" and \"there was no chain\" are different facts about a route, and\nonly the first tells you your fallbacks are configured.\n\n`_apply_message_routing_policies` rebuilt the plan positionally, which would\nhave dropped both new fields for every safety-classifier request; it uses\n`dataclasses.replace` now.\n\nSurfaced in three places:\n\n- The request detail draws the chain as a path, each hop marked answered /\n  failed / not needed, in words as well as colour, with a sentence naming what\n  the request was diverted from and why.\n- A Vision adapter panel beside Failover, with the same from -> to shape.\n- A `vision` badge on the model cell in the table, next to the existing\n  fallback badge.\n\n`stats()` gains `diverted` and `diverted_routes` alongside the fallback pair.\n\n**gpt-5.6 is a family name, not a servable id.** Only -luna, -sol and -terra\nexist on this plan; the bare id 404s. 4.41.0 removed an explicit exclusion for\nit on the grounds that it contradicted the provider's own \">5.4\" heuristic --\nthe heuristic was the thing that was wrong, and the original author knew. It is\nback in the disallow set, with the three real variants in the static list.\n\nVerification:\n- A real 3-hop chain end to end against a live server: two broken NVIDIA models\n  then `opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free`. The row records all three hops in\n  order with `route_attempt=2`, and `route_chain[route_attempt]` equals\n  `provider/resolved_model`.\n- A real image request end to end: `nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free` publishes\n  `input_modalities: [\"text\"]`, the request diverted, and the row carries\n  `route_diverted_from=nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free`, `route_diversion=vision`.\n  `stats()` reports `diverted=1` with the from -> to pair. (The upstream then\n  400'd because the adapter model chosen for the test cannot read images\n  either -- which is the diversion being visible, not the diversion failing.)\n- The dashboard renderers driven through jsdom against real row shapes: 20\n  checks covering hop marking, the untried tail, the diversion note, the empty\n  panel, both badges, and rows written before route tracing.\n- Full suite: 3345 passed, 6 failed -- the PowerShell installer baseline.\n  ruff format, ruff check and ty clean.\n\nNot verified: no browser. The chain block's spacing and colour are reasoned\nabout, not seen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
